# This file limits the Docker build context to what the Dockerfile copies.
#
# Everything is excluded by default, then the Dockerfile's COPY sources are
# re-included. A new file or directory under app/ stays out of the build
# context, and out of the published image, until it is listed here. When the
# Dockerfile gains a COPY, add its source below.
#
# Docker still sends Dockerfile and .dockerignore to the builder, because the
# build needs them, but no COPY can reach them.
#
# Later patterns override earlier ones, so the exclusions at the end must stay
# after the re-includes.
#
# More information on using .dockerignore is available here:
# https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#dockerignore-files

*

# Mix project and the config the prod build reads (dev.exs and test.exs stay out)
!/mix.exs
!/mix.lock
!/config/config.exs
!/config/prod.exs
!/config/runtime.exs

# Application source, assets, and release files
!/lib
!/priv
!/assets
!/rel

# Static artifacts - These should be fetched and built inside the Docker image
# https://phoenix.hexdocs.pm/Mix.Tasks.Phx.Gen.Release.html#module-docker
/assets/node_modules/
/priv/static/assets/
/priv/static/cache_manifest.json

# Dev-only files under priv/, which the release would otherwise ship whole:
# the Dialyzer PLTs and the seed script with its fixed dev login.
/priv/plts/
/priv/repo/seeds.exs

# Env files at any depth, samples included: local settings and the production
# secrets `just fly-secrets` reads from .env.prod. The release takes its
# settings from the container environment, so the builder never needs them.
**/.env*

# CI workflow definition. It lives at the repository root, outside this build
# context, so this only keeps out a copy that lands under app/.
**/goodflows.toml

# Finder metadata inside the re-included directories
**/.DS_Store
